# orchestrator.conf — per-operator identity for this derailleur instance.
#
# Copy this file to `orchestrator.conf` (gitignored) and fill in your own values.
# The scripts source it to learn who they're running as, so a labmate can run
# their own instance without editing any code:
#
#     cp orchestrator.conf.example orchestrator.conf
#     $EDITOR orchestrator.conf
#
# Every field is required; a script aborts with guidance if any is left blank.
# Shell-sourced, so quote values with spaces and don't put a space around `=`.

# Display name of the human operator. Used in the orchestrator/checker briefs
# ("the orchestrator for <name>'s research work") and the board digest's
# "Needs <name>" section header. Free text — spaces are fine.
OPERATOR_NAME="Your Name"

# Your GitHub handle WITHOUT the leading @. Used to @-mention you in the
# escalation comments workers/checkers post when they hand a decision back.
GITHUB_HANDLE="your-handle"

# GitHub owner (user or org) whose issues/PRs this instance dispatches against.
# Passed to `gh search --owner`. Usually the same string as GITHUB_HANDLE.
PR_OWNER="your-handle"

# launchd job label for the scheduled loop (reverse-DNS style, no spaces). Names
# the LaunchAgent installed into ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ by `schedule.sh install`
# and the plist rendered from host/LaunchAgents/orchestrator.plist.
LAUNCHD_LABEL="com.your-handle.orchestrator"

# Your cross-repo GitHub Projects board number (the "N" in
# `gh project view N --owner @me`). board-digest.sh reads this board to build the
# orchestrator's dispatchable view. Find it with `gh project list --owner @me`.
BOARD_PROJECT="1"

# --- Optional -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Model for the HEADLESS/autonomous orchestrator (orchestrator-cycle.sh, whether
# cron- or hand-triggered). It only reads the board digest and routes, so it's
# pinned cheap. Resolution order is: MODEL env var → this field → sonnet, so an
# explicit `MODEL=… dr orchestrator-cycle` still overrides. Optional: absence
# defaults to sonnet and never fails the identity guard. This does NOT affect the
# INTERACTIVE orchestrator (launch-orchestrator.sh / /orchestrate), which stays on
# the human-present session's model.
#
# ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL="sonnet"

# Dispatch schedule — the SINGLE source of truth for when the scheduled loop fires.
# Space-separated 24h HH:MM slots (zero-padded). `schedule.sh install` derives BOTH
# the launchd fire times (StartCalendarInterval) AND the pmset wake chain from this
# one value, so changing the cadence is a one-line edit here followed by
# `./bin/schedule.sh install` — no hand-editing of the plist or the script.
#
# Slots are treated as the desired fire CENTERS shifted 15 min early: run-cycle.sh's
# --jitter then sleeps 0–30 min so each cycle lands within ±15 min of its center
# (de-syncing from other hosts' on-the-hour cron). SLOTS[0] also seeds the daily
# pmset repeat-wake. If unset, defaults to the night-heavy schedule below (centers
# 20/23/02/05/08). For an hourly cadence: "00:00 01:00 02:00 ... 23:00".
#
# SCHEDULE_SLOTS="19:45 22:45 01:45 04:45 07:45"
